Add algebra::structure pass

Add a Rust-side reimplementation of the eqlog.eql Structure/El/pred_app
/func_app/var/el-type machinery in `eqlog/src/algebra/structure.rs`.

A `Structure` carries a flat `Vec<El>` (each El holding an optional
TypeId plus a parent model el chain), a `BTreeSet<PredApp>`, and a
`BTreeMap<FuncApp, ElId>`. PredApp and FuncApp are data-keyed structs
holding the pred/func id, its parent model el chain, and its argument
els.

`build_structures` walks each rule body and assigns a before- and
after-structure to every statement. The after is produced by cloning
the before and extending it with whatever the statement introduces.
No morphisms, no unification, no equating of elements. Match scrutinee
and pattern terms are walked into their branch's starting structure.

The pass surfaces ambient-resolved FunctionArgumentNumber and
PredicateArgumentNumber errors. Member-resolved references are skipped
because resolving them requires type inference on the receiver term,
which this pass does not do.

Also widens `algebra::signature::Signature` with PredDeclId -> PredId,
FuncDeclId -> FuncId, CtorDeclId -> FuncId lookups and Type/Pred/Func
data accessors the structure pass needs.
